  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oracle Health Government Services has $2.1B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Oracle Health Government Services received 30 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $68.8M and obligations up 105.0% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a path of variation: FY21 was $971M, FY22 was $2B, FY23 was $825M, FY24 was $893M, FY25 was $1B, and FY26 is $2.1B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buying agency, having obligated $2.1B. Computer Systems Design Services is the top market for Oracle Health Government Services, with $2.1B in obligations; smaller markets listed include Computer Facilities Management Services at $3.6M and Used Household and Office Goods Moving at $110K. The report uses contract obligations for most figures and notes that some largest-awards and expiring-contracts entries, when present, are total contract values rather than obligations. This snapshot covers fiscal year to date activity only; current-year totals are partial.",
